    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:d1bf136a4a3c936a",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "578159ea034e36b0f78876fef2c685b71c567a336902243da0f356da6c26fff5",
      "text": "After breakfast, head into the high Venezuelan Andes. On the way, visit Capilla de Piedras, a stone chapel and monument. Lunch at Casa de Pastel is payable separately.\n\nFrom Mucubají Lagoon, walk to the glacial Laguna Negra at 3,500 m. If you prefer, you can ride a mule for part of the way for USD 10, payable on site. Along the trail, tropical vegetation gives way to high-altitude lichens and mosses. The surrounding mountains and El Águila peak are reflected in the lagoon's dark water. Check in at the hotel and rest.\n\nMeals: breakfast.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-a14d0606-b6fe-4d7e-a104-240f602fd877",
        "model": "GPT-6.1",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The Word splits the chapel and lagoon across separate days, describes an optional horseback ride and has no passage for this walking route, mule option, price or hotel sequence."
      }
